.SH NAME
inspekt\-sr \- Screen reader simulation commands.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]sr\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]SUBCOMMAND\f[R]
[\f[I]ARGS\f[R]]\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Screen reader simulation commands.
.PP
Simulate how JAWS, NVDA, and VoiceOver would announce page content.
Uses announcement patterns sourced from the W3C ARIA\-AT project and
a11ysupport.io to approximate real screen reader behavior.
.PP
\f[B]Subcommands:\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]walk\f[R]: Walk through the page in reading order, showing
announcements
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]compare\f[R]: Side\-by\-side comparison of all three screen
readers
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]announce\f[R]: Announce a specific element
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
